From aceac20d5faf0f75125a6694fe1cc91557f994c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 05:52:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] AB monitor 1.7.0: interactive pyqtgraph GUI plots
 (ab_live_plots 0.1.0)

* GUI: one tab per meter, one plot per unit (or per table / overlay group),
  crosshair shared by the meter's plots, legend column with value at cursor
  and newest value, zoom/pan while updating (Ctrl+wheel, drag), follow
  newest with window presets, identity line (reported address, serial),
  gaps for outages; matplotlib picture previews kept as fallback
  (PREVIEW_BACKEND, missing pyqtgraph, failed start-up check).
* Monitor API: preview_groups(), preview_meter_ips(), meter_identity();
  poll_cycle() status gains reported_ips; LIVE_PLOT_* switches.
* Memory: curves updated in place; hidden tabs release arrays; pyqtgraph
  menus deleted with their plot (PySide6 6.2 leak); clear() instead of
  setData([], []).
* Python 3.7: PySide6 6.2.4 + pyqtgraph 0.12.4; requirements and kit spec
  (pyqtgraph 0.14.0) updated; install.sh 1.2.1 installs ab_live_plots.py.
* Tests: test_live_plots.py (8 checks), live_plot_memory_check.py, GUI soak
  0.0.3 (fails on silent fallback), runner 0.0.4 (+ live_plots, 3.7 package
  detection). run_all_tests --quick 11/11 on 3.12.3 and 3.7.12.
* Docs: README, manual (LuaLaTeX), Windows START_HERE 1.2.0, plan 0.0.2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
