+\section{GUI}\label{sec:gui}
+The window holds the output and memory-protection controls, the memory line,
+the bounded status console and the plots. The View menu toggles light and
+dark themes; the plots follow the theme. Closing the window waits for the
 final writes instead of terminating the worker thread.
 
+\subsection{Interactive plots (1.7.0)}
+Up to 1.6.5 the GUI showed one matplotlib picture per tab (one tab per table
+and per overlay group, about 40 tabs for two meters); reading a number meant
+opening a frozen copy in a separate window. Since 1.7.0 the plots are drawn
+by pyqtgraph~\cite{pyqtgraph} through the companion module
+\code{ab_live_plots.py} (Fig.~\ref{fig:gui}):
+
+\begin{itemize}
+  \item \textbf{One tab per meter.} At the top, the meter's identity line:
+        polled address, the address the meter reports on its page~1 (red when
+        it differs), serial number, rows in memory, and whether it answered
+        the last poll.
+  \item \textbf{One plot per unit} (V, A, W, VAR, VA, \%, Hz, kWh, \dots) with
+        every parameter of that unit as a trace --- the grouping of the
+        Grafana dashboard. The \emph{View} box offers \emph{by table} (one
+        plot per table and unit) and \emph{overlay groups}.
+  \item \textbf{Crosshair and legend column.} The mouse over any plot places
+        a crosshair in every plot of the meter (their time axes are linked).
+        Beside each plot a table lists every trace with a tick box (hide or
+        show), its value \emph{at the cursor} (nearest sample; ``-'' inside a
+        gap) and its \emph{newest} value. The legend has its own column, so
+        it never covers the newest data.
+  \item \textbf{Zoom and pan while updating.} Curves are updated in place
+        (\code{setData}~\cite{pyqtgraph_pdi}), so the view is kept. Left drag
+        pans, right drag zooms one axis, Ctrl\,+\,wheel zooms; a plain wheel
+        scrolls the tab (\code{LIVE_PLOT_WHEEL_NEEDS_CTRL}). Any manual zoom
+        or pan switches \emph{Follow newest} off, so a poll never moves the
+        view from under the mouse; \emph{Show} selects the follow window
+        (10~min \dots\ 7~d, all). The right-click menu exports a plot as
+        CSV, PNG or SVG.
+  \item \textbf{Gaps.} A time step longer than \code{LIVE_PLOT_GAP_FACTOR}
+        (3) times the median step is drawn as a gap instead of a line.
+\end{itemize}
+
