+\paragraph{Data path and memory.} The plots never touch the store directly:
+after a poll, only the \emph{visible} meter tab calls
+\code{preview_groups(ip, view)}, which copies that meter's lists under the
+store lock, converts them to NumPy outside it and min/max-decimates each
+trace to \code{LIVE_PLOT_MAX_POINTS} (10\,000; a one-sample spike survives);
+pyqtgraph thins further to the screen (peak downsampling, clip to view).
+Hidden tabs drop their arrays (\code{LIVE_PLOT_RELEASE_HIDDEN}) and are
+refilled when shown. Table~\ref{tab:livemem} gives the cost for one emulated
+meter (44 traces).
+
+\begin{table}[ht]
+  \centering
+  \caption{Cost of one meter's plots (\code{tests/live_plot_memory_check.py};
+  Python 3.12.3 / 3.7.12). ``Arrays'' is Python and NumPy memory held by the
+  tab (tracemalloc); after hiding, 2.2\,MB of pyqtgraph objects remain.}
+  \label{tab:livemem}
+  \begin{tabular}{@{}rrrrr@{}}
+    \toprule
+    Rows per table & Store (MB) & Update after a poll (s) & Arrays (MB) & Hidden (MB) \\
+    \midrule
+    1\,000 & 3.4 & 0.03 / 0.02 & 2.7 & 2.2 \\
+    10\,000 & 33.7 & 0.06 / 0.05 & 6.4 & 2.2 \\
+    50\,000 & 168.6 & 0.30 / 0.25 & 9.0 & 2.2 \\
+    \bottomrule
+  \end{tabular}
+\end{table}
+
+\paragraph{Two leaks found and fixed.} (1) pyqtgraph builds the right-click
+menus of every plot without a Qt parent; with PySide6~6.2 they outlived the
+deleted plot (11 per plot, 351 per change of view). They are now deleted with
+the plot. (2) Emptying a curve with \code{setData([], [])} leaves pyqtgraph's
+inner curve holding its last display arrays (views of the whole trace,
+6.9\,MB at 50\,000 rows); a hidden tab now calls \code{clear()}.
+
+\paragraph{Fallback.} With \code{PREVIEW_BACKEND = "matplotlib"}, without
+pyqtgraph, or when pyqtgraph fails a start-up check (one plot is built and
+deleted: pyqtgraph~0.12.4 imports with PySide6~$\ge$~6.3 but fails as soon
+as a plot is built), the GUI shows the 1.6 picture previews and logs a
+WARNING.
+
+\paragraph{Python versions.} pyqtgraph 0.14.0 needs Python~$\ge$~3.10,
+0.13.3 is the last for 3.8 and 0.12.4 the last for 3.7~\cite{pyqtgraph_pypi};
+0.12.4 works only with PySide6~$\le$~6.2.4, so \code{requirements-py37.txt}
+pins PySide6~6.2.4 (was 6.5.3). \code{tests/test_live_plots.py} passed on
+3.12.3 (PySide6 6.12.0 and 6.11.2), 3.8.20 (PySide6 6.6.3.1) and 3.7.12
+(PySide6 6.2.4).
+
